-- 0256: fold every place filed TWICE UNDER ONE PARENT into one area ("The Pawn" / "Pawn, The").
--
-- Asked: "keep going" (2026-10-07), under the standing rule "fold into 1 area, same for everything
-- else, i don't want duplicates". Found while settling "2. Microagression" (0254 held it): Long Hill
-- Conservation Area is a second copy of Hidden in Plain Sight Boulders — its First..Fourth Boulder hold
-- the same problems at the same grades (Megaman V3, Dick Move V1-2, Party Foul V3+, Phlebotomy Crack
-- V2-3, Microagression V4), under another parent 4 km off. Looking for the class: check:area-duplicates
-- SKIPS two areas under the SAME parent, and 209 same-parent groups share its name key — nearly all one
-- import's "Pawn, The" beside another's "The Pawn" at the same coordinate (The Needles of Rushmore 1,503
-- climbs + 33, The Tennessee Wall, The Callahans, The Near Trapps, The Lost Sierra ...), plus "Mount X" /
-- "Mt. X", "X" / "X Area", and an ICE-tree copy of a crag ("Catskills (Ice)", "Palisade Head ICE").
--
-- Read (2026-10-07), each group with any distance between its members climb by climb. NOT folded:
-- Index / Mount Index, Baker Crags / Mount Baker, Mount Wilson / Wilson Peak (two peaks), Jump For Jesus
-- (0251 read it as a formation inside its area). Brink's Rock is a crag INSIDE Brink's Rock Area: nested
-- there, its name kept. Poke-O-Moonshine's two copies in the Adirondack ICE tree (one with no coordinate,
-- which is why no guard saw it) join the rock crag. No contribution, log, photo, topo or list points at
-- any climb deleted. Plan: the most climbs is kept; each copy folds in (0251's fold, recursively):
--   * 219 climbs stored on both sides — the keeper fills each BLANK column from the copy (0221's
--     rule) and the copy row is deleted. Same name, same base grade, compatible discipline; or, across the
--     two copies of one wall, a placeholder ("Unknown 5.5") with the SAME grade; or 15 read by hand —
--     one import carries the FA, the other the pitches and length, the grades drifted ("The Mordor Wall"
--     5.6 / 5.7 A3): the higher grade is kept (owner rule: never lower a grade).
--   * 215 other climbs move into the keeper; 2 share a name with a DIFFERENT climb there
--     ("unknown" 5.8+ / 5.9 — placeholders with different grades stay two) and move with the trigger bypassed.
--   * 81 sub-areas re-parented; a sub-area whose twin is under the keeper folds the same way.
--   * 243 emptied copies deleted, children first; the keeper first fills its blank columns from them.
--   * 7 groups list climbs flat in one member and sub-areas in the other: see step 2.
--   * 127 keepers renamed: "Pawn, The" -> "The Pawn"; "Catskills (Ice)" -> "Catskills" once it holds
--     the rock climbs too. 1 climb renamed: "2. Microagression" -> "Microagression", its twin gone.
-- ABORTS if climber data points at a climb deleted (an area's photos move to the keeper), or if the live tree no longer matches the plan.
-- Plan: the job's fold2/plan.mjs (log reviewed); rollback: scripts/data/area-twin-folds-rollback.json.
-- APPLIED LIVE BY HAND 2026-10-07 as "0255" — but #2249 had just recorded 0255 (areas_carry_parking), so
-- the hand apply's record hit `on conflict do nothing` and this was renumbered 0256. The merge replays it
-- once: the first guard finds no copy area and returns, every update and delete is keyed to rows that are
-- gone, the final check passes on the keepers already in place — a no-op that records 0256 (dry-run so).

begin;

create temp table m_merge(keep text not null, drop_id text primary key, grade text, disc text) on commit drop;

create temp table m_route_rename(id text primary key, from_name text not null, to_name text not null) on commit drop;

create temp table m_move(id text primary key, from_area text not null, to_area text not null, bypass boolean not null) on commit drop;

create temp table m_reparent(id text primary key, from_area text not null, to_area text not null) on commit drop;

create temp table m_drop_area(id text primary key, into_area text not null, ord int not null) on commit drop;

create temp table m_rename(id text primary key, from_name text not null, to_name text not null, bypass boolean not null) on commit drop;

create temp table m_rename_first(id text primary key, from_name text not null, to_name text not null) on commit drop;

-- every ancestor of every touched area, read BEFORE anything moves (old and new ancestors both)
